# SDD Micro

Tiny/personal projects only — 3 commands, no BRD/UC/SRD/Validate/
Analyze/Clarify/Design/Release ceremony. See `CLAUDE.md` for why.

## Startup (every session)
Read these files in order before doing anything else:
1. `.specify/manifest.yml` — project name, feature, workflow mode
2. `.specify/memory/constitution.md` — universal rules (Part 1) + project tech stack (Part 2)

Confirm: project.name, feature, constitution status (GATE-1 confirmed?).
If constitution Part 2 is a DRAFT (not confirmed) → remind the user to
say "confirmed" before /task.

## Running Commands
To run any SDD command, read and follow the matching prompt file **exactly as written**:

| Command | Prompt File |
|---|---|
| create-context *(optional)* | `.github/prompts/create-context.prompt.md` |
| specify | `.github/prompts/specify.prompt.md` |
| task | `.github/prompts/task.prompt.md` |
| implement | `.github/prompts/implement.prompt.md` |

**How to invoke in Cursor:** In the chat panel, type:
`Read and follow .github/prompts/specify.prompt.md exactly`

## Command Order
SPECIFY → [GATE-1: confirmed] → TASK → IMPLEMENT

## Never Do
- Never run /task before constitution Part 2 is confirmed (GATE-1)
- Never run /implement without a tasks.md the user has seen
- Never hardcode secrets or credentials
- Never skip the verification step named in a task
